  "package_manifest_sha256": "ad12a6de63ea5f0044bd38798c816771e511dac75eea84bb0fb2217a704a8cff",
  "credential_check": "No auth.json, .credentials.json or .claude.json member and no symlink; all 394 members are session .jsonl files under home/.claude/projects, 48 root and 346 subagent transcripts. A token-pattern search (Anthropic and OpenAI keys, Bearer headers, OAuth token fields, credentials.json content, GitHub and GitLab tokens, AWS keys, Slack tokens and webhooks, Google API keys, JWTs, private keys) and an exact search for the values of the signed-in account file and credentials file matched no credential. The JWT search matched two strings that the task packets already hold: the Netlify bot's deploy-preview QR-code image path in the r-base-ui-5460 attempts att-010, att-026 and att-042, and the Vercel bot comment's metadata in the j-trpc-5017 attempts att-002, att-018 and att-034. Neither is a credential. Every transcript carries the account email in the client's userEmail context and the organization UUID in a credential_org attachment, as the earlier public Claude transcript releases do: the published 2026-10-28-claude-ce-opus-selected/att-001 archive carries both in the same places. Every transcript also carries the run host's login name, in working-directory paths and project-directory names, as that earlier archive does. No account UUID, user ID, account name, organization name or plan identifier is present.",
